# Copy to .env.local.
#
# The marketing page renders with none of these set — every content getter falls
# back to the launch copy in src/lib/*. But that is the ONLY thing that survives
# an empty environment:
#
#   - /admin throws "missing secret key" without PAYLOAD_SECRET, and
#   - `payload migrate` in the deploy build needs both it and DATABASE_URI, and
#   - a production build with no DATABASE_URI bakes the fallback copy into the
#     static page and still reports success, so the deploy goes green while the
#     site quietly ignores the CMS.
#
# On Vercel these must be available to the BUILD step, not just at runtime: the
# home page is prerendered.

# --- Payload CMS (content only: portfolio, testimonials, FAQs, page copy) ---
# This site's own Postgres. It holds content, never bookings.
# Use a Neon branch for local work — pointing .env.local at the production
# database means every local edit and seed writes to the live site's content.
DATABASE_URI=
# openssl rand -hex 32 — and mint a SEPARATE one for production. This key signs
# admin sessions, so a shared value makes a laptop's .env.local able to forge a
# production admin session.
PAYLOAD_SECRET=

# Public origin, used for canonical URLs, OpenGraph and JSON-LD. Set it to the
# real domain in production; a wrong value only affects those tags, never the
# admin. (It is deliberately NOT handed to Payload as `serverURL` — pinning
# Payload to one origin makes every admin save 403 on any other host, silently.)
NEXT_PUBLIC_SERVER_URL=http://localhost:3000

# Optional. Only consulted on preview deployments, where the real URL is not
# known until the build starts; ignored in production so a deploy-unique host
# can never land in the canonical tag. Vercel does not set this for you.
NEXT_PUBLIC_VERCEL_URL=

# --- Bookings API (commerce lives here, not in this app) -------------------
# Server-side only. Never expose as NEXT_PUBLIC_*: this key can create bookings.
SENTRY_API_BASE=
SENTRY_BOOKINGS_KEY=

# --- Transactional email (studio-branded, sent from this app) --------------
RESEND_API_KEY=

# --- Media storage for CMS uploads ------------------------------------------
# NOT WIRED UP YET. No storage adapter is installed, so Payload writes uploads
# to the local media/ directory — which is ephemeral on Vercel and loses every
# uploaded photo on the next deploy. Setting this token alone changes nothing;
# it needs @payloadcms/storage-vercel-blob (or the R2 adapter) in the config.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=

# --- Protects the confirm-poller cron route --------------------------------
CRON_SECRET=
